  <reason>Subject and account: The subject of this report is Usman Hassan, holder of account PK**HABB****2657, opened on 25 November 2022. The customer's declared occupation is student, with a declared income of PKR 30,000 per month.

Activity summary: During the period 1 May 2026 to 9 May 2026, the account recorded 21 credits totalling PKR 1,367,000 as well as 5 debits totalling PKR 1,331,000. The credits arrived as 21 interbank (IBFT) transfers from 15 distinct senders. The activity was detected on 9 May 2026, when Tazama typology MULE-01 scored 360 against an alert threshold of 300.

Grounds for suspicion: The account received funds from 15 distinct senders within the activity window. Funds did not remain in the account: debits equal to 97% of credits, with a median of 1.7 hours between the latest credit and each debit. For a customer whose declared occupation is student, credits in the activity window were 45.6 times the declared monthly income, against a declared income of PKR 30,000 per month. A note by Fraud Desk (9 May 2026): "Two sender banks raised fraud recall requests against inbound transfers to this account, citing scam complaints." Taken together, these indicators are consistent with suspected money mule activity; the reporting entity has not established the underlying offence.

Flow of funds: Of the outgoing funds, PKR 688,000 was sent to QuickPay wallet ***0932 (WLT****0932, Synthetic EMI) in 3 transactions. Of the outgoing funds, PKR 643,000 was withdrawn as Cash (ATM) in 2 transactions.

Other considerations: Screening of the subject returned no match on sanctions, PEP or adverse-media screening on 28 May 2026.

Action taken by the reporting entity: Action taken: a note by L2 analyst (11 May 2026): "Outgoing wallet transfers placed on hold pending review. No contact made with the customer about this review."</reason>
